{
  "summary": "Introduces a named constant `Sock::MAX_WAIT_TIMEOUT` (about 24.8 days in whole seconds) for the socket wait timeout cap introduced in PR 36340, and documents the cap in `Sock::Wait()` and `WaitMany()`. In `bitcoin-cli`, it replaces a 5-year timeout fallback for `-rpcclienttimeout=0` with `Sock::MAX_WAIT_TIMEOUT` and updates the CLI help text to specify that 0 sets the longest supported timeout (~24 days) rather than no timeout.",
  "problem": "PR 36340 capped socket wait times to `INT_MAX` milliseconds to prevent `select()` overflow crashes on macOS, leaving an undocumented inline magic number in `Sock::WaitMany`. Furthermore, `bitcoin-cli` documented `-rpcclienttimeout=0` as \"no timeout\" while passing an arbitrary 5-year duration that was already capped at ~24.8 days by the socket layer on every wait.",
  "evidence": [
    "Addresses review comments from #36340 where reviewers noted that capping socket wait timeouts was undocumented in caller headers and left bitcoin-cli's 5-year placeholder misleading (description).",
    "Description notes this is a refactoring and documentation follow-up with 'no behaviour change'."
